# Every text file is checked out with LF on every platform.  The receipts of
# the pinned library products, the ICurry cache and the overlay archives key
# on the bytes of the sources, and the Windows default of CRLF on checkout
# made every receipt differ (the Windows spike, 2026-10-29).  Git tells a
# binary by its content; the known binary kinds are marked anyway.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.tgz -text
*.gz -text
*.z -text
*.png -text
*.ico -text
*.whl -text
*.so -text
*.dylib -text
*.dll -text
*.exe -text
*.pdf -text
# Eight test programs arrived from upstream with CRLF, and the receipts of
# their products in the overlay archive were taken on those bytes: they
# keep them on every platform.
tests/data/curry/benchmarks/PokerFree.curry -text
tests/data/curry/benchmarks/failing/sendMoreMoney.curry -text
